### Findings worth keeping

- **Headless Chrome floors `--window-size` below ~500px CSS width** and resamples the
  PNG, so narrow "mobile" screenshots taken that way are silently wrong. Every
  viewport claim in this run is now made through `shot.mjs`, which uses
  `Emulation.setDeviceMetricsOverride` and asserts `innerWidth === requested`.
- **`--force-dark-mode` does not drive `prefers-color-scheme`** — it is Chromium's
  auto-darkening filter. `--blink-settings=preferredColorScheme=0|1` does.
- Chrome resolves a missing audio file and an undecodable one to the same
  `MEDIA_ERR_SRC_NOT_SUPPORTED`; the control handles both without needing to tell
  them apart.

## Two modes: two art directions, confirmed

Not one palette inverted. Dark carries layered radial light pools, gradient-faded
dividers, an inset top highlight on raised surfaces, and a soft bloom on focus.
Light carries a flat fill with 5% SVG paper grain, hairline dividers, flat borders,
zero shadow, and no bloom. Both were rendered and measured separately.

